{title: Trumpets, Jars and Torches}
{subtitle: Judges 6:11–16; 6:36–40; 7:2–7; 7:16–22}
{key: C}
{tempo: 119}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] | [C] | [F] [G] | [C] |
| [F] [G] [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Gideon was hiding, threshing [F]wheat where none could [C]see
[F]Scared of all [C]the Midianites, like [Dm]locusts on the [G]trees
Then an [F]angel sat beneath [G]the oak and [Em]said to [Am]him
The [F]LORD is with you, [G]mighty war[C]rior
Who, me? said Gideon, I [F]am the least of [C]all
But [F]God said, I [C]will be with you, and [G]God is never small
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]Blow your trumpet, toot toot toot
[F]Smash your jar, [C]crash crash crash
Hold your torch up shining bright
[Dm]A sword for the LORD [G]and for Gideon
[F]God can [G]win with [Em]just a [Am]few
[F]When we trust him, [G]me and [C]you [F][G]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Gideon was nervous, so he [F]laid a woolly [C]fleece
On the [F]threshing floor at [C]night and said, [Dm]God, show me [G]please
In the [F]morning, wet [G]fleece, and the [Em]ground was dry all [Am]round
[F]Next night, dry fleece, [G]and dew on all the [C]ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Thir-ty-two thousand soldiers came [F]to stand at Gideon's [C]side
[F]Too many, said the [C]LORD, or [Dm]they will boast in [G]pride
[F]Down to ten [G]thousand, then [Em]down to the stream they [Am]went
Three [F]hundred lapped the water, and [G]those were the ones God [C]sent
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Blow your trumpet, toot toot toot
[F]Smash your jar, [C]crash crash crash
Hold your torch up shining bright
[Dm]A sword for the LORD [G]and for Gideon
[F]God can [G]win with [Em]just a [Am]few
[F]When we trust him, [G]me and [C]you [F]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[G]One [C]hundred, two hundred, three [F]hundred [C]men
All around the camp in the [Dm]dark [G]night
[F]Ready, [G]steady, [Em]blow, smash, [Am]shine
And the [F]LORD [G]made it [C]right
{end_of_bridge}

{comment: Outro}
